#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "&turtlescript; Programming Reference"
msgstr "&turtlescript; Referenca Programiranja"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the reference for &kturtle;'s &turtlescript;. In the first section "
"of this chapter have a look at some aspects of the <link linkend=\"grammar"
"\">grammar</link> of &turtlescript; programs. The second section deals "
"exclusively with <link linkend=\"mathematical-operators\">mathematical "
"operators</link>, <link linkend=\"boolean-operators\">boolean (true/false) "
"operators</link> and <link linkend=\"comparing-operators\">comparison "
"operators</link>. The third section is basically a giant list of all <link "
"linkend=\"commands\">commands</link> explaining them one-by-one. Section "
"four explains how to <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">assign</link> "
"values to <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">variables</link>. "
"Finally we explain how to arrange the execution of commands with <link "
"linkend=\"controlling-execution\">execution controlling statements</link> in "
"section five and how to create you own commands with <link linkend=\"learn"
"\">learn</link> in section six."
msgstr ""
"Ovo je referenca za &kturtle;'s &turtlescript;. U prvom odjeljku ovog "
"odlomka pogedajte neke aspekte <link linkend=\"grammar\">gramatika</link> "
"&turtlescript; programa. Drugi odjeljak bavi se isključivo sa <link linkend="
"\"mathematical-operators\">matematički operatori</link>, <link linkend="
"\"boolean-operators\">boolean (tačno/pogrešno) operatori</link> i <link "
"linkend=\"comparing-operators\">operatori poređenja</link>. Treći odjeljak "
"je u osnovi ogromna lista svih <link linkend=\"commands\">komandi</link> "
"objašnjavajući ih jednu po jednu. Odjeljak četiri objašnjava kako <link "
"linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">dodijeliti</link> vrijednosti <link "
"linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">varijablama</link>. Konačno mi "
"objašnjavamo kako urediti izvršenje komandi sa <link linkend=\"controlling-"
"execution\">izjavama ze kontrolisanje izvršenja</link> u odjeljku pet i kako "
"da napravite vaše vlastite komande sa <link linkend=\"learn\">učenjem </"
"link> u odjeljku šest."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Grammar of &turtlescript;"
msgstr "Gramatika &turtlescript;"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As in any language, &turtlescript; has different types of words and symbols. "
"In English we distinguish verbs (like 'to walk' or 'to sing') and nouns "
"(like 'sister' or 'house'), they are used for different purposes. "
"&turtlescript; is a programming language, it is used to instruct &kturtle; "
"what to do."
msgstr ""
"Kao u svakom jeziku, &turtlescript; ima različite tipove riječi i simbola. U "
"engleskom jeziku mi razlikujemo glagole (poput 'šetati' ili 'pjevati') i "
"imenice (kao 'sestra' ili 'kuća'), oni se koriste u različite svrhe. "
"&turtlescript; je programski jezik, koristi se da instruira &kturtle; šta da "
"radi."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section some of &turtlescript;'s different types of words and "
"symbols are briefly explained. We explain <link linkend=\"comment"
"\">comments</link>, <link linkend=\"command\">commands</link> and the three "
"different kinds of literals: <link linkend=\"number\">numbers</link>, <link "
"linkend=\"string\">strings</link> and <link linkend=\"boolean-value"
"\">boolean (true/false) values</link>."
msgstr ""
"U ovom odjeljku neki od različitih tipova riječi i simbola &turtlescript; -a "
"su ukratko objašnjeni. Mi objašnjavamo <link linkend=\"comment\">komentare</"
"link>, <link linkend=\"command\">komande</link> i tri različita tipa "
"literala: <link linkend=\"number\">brojevi</link>, <link linkend=\"string"
"\">stringovi</link> i <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulove (tačno/"
"pogrešno) vrijednosti</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Komentari"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A program consists instructions that are executed when the program is run "
"and so called comments. Comments are not executed, &kturtle; simply ignores "
"them when executing your program. Comment are there for other programmers to "
"make them understand your program better. Everything that follows on a "
"<userinput>#</userinput> symbol is considered a comment in &turtlescript;. "
"For example this little program that does nothing: <screen>\n"
"# this little program does nothing, it is only a comment!\n"
"</screen> It is a bit useless but it explain the matter well."
msgstr ""
"Program sadrži instrukcije koje se izvrše kada se program pokrene i tzv. "
"komentare. Komentari se ne izvršavaju, &kturtle; ih jednostavno ignoriše "
"kada izvršava vaš program. Komentarari su tu za druge programere kako bi "
"bolje razumjeli vaš program. Sve što slijedi na <userinput>#</userinput> "
"simbolu smatra se komentarom u &turtlescript;. Na primjer ovaj mali program "
"koji ništa ne radi: <screen>\n"
"# ovaj mali program ne radi ništa, on je samo komentar!\n"
"</screen> On je pomalo beskoristan ali dobro objašnjava stvari."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Comments get very useful when the program gets a little bit more complex. It "
"can help to give some advice to other programmers. In the following program "
"you see comments being used together with the <link linkend=\"print\">print</"
"link> command. <screen>\n"
"# this program has been made by Cies Breijs.\n"
"print \"this text will get printed on the canvas\"\n"
"# the previous line is not a comment, but the next line is:\n"
"# print \"this text will not get printed!\"\n"
"</screen> The first line describes the program. The second line is executed "
"by &kturtle; and prints <userinput>this text will get printed on the canvas</"
"userinput> on the canvas. The third line is a comment. And the forth line is "
"a comment that contains a piece of &turtlescript;, if the <userinput>#</"
"userinput> symbol would be removed on the fourth line the print statement "
"will we executed by &kturtle;. Programmers say: the print statement on the "
"fourth line is 'commented out'."
msgstr ""
"Komentari postaju vrlo korisni kada program postaje malo kompleksniji. Može "
"pomoći da pruži neki savjet drugim programerima. U sljedećem programu vidite "
"komentare koji se koriste zajedno sa <link linkend=\"print\">štampaj</link> "
"komandom. <screen>\n"
"# ovaj program napravio je Cies Breijs.\n"
"štampaj \"ovaj tekst bit će štampan na platnu\"\n"
"# prethodni red nije komentar, ali naredni red jeste:\n"
"# štampaj \"ovaj tekst neće biti štampan!\".\n"
"</screen> Prva linija opisuje program. Drugu liniju izvodi &kturtle; i "
"prikazuje <userinput>ovaj tekst bit će štampan na platnu</userinput> na "
"platnu. Treća linija je komentar. Četvrta linija je komentar koja sadrži dio "
"&turtlescript;, ako se<userinput>#</userinput> simbol ukloni na četvrtoj "
"liniji, naredba štampanja će biti izvršena od strane &kturtle;. Programeri "
"kažu, četvrta linija je dekomentirana."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Commented lines are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with light gray in "
"the <link linkend=\"the-editor\">code editor</link>."
msgstr ""
"Komentarisani redovi su <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> sa svijetlo sivim "
"u <link linkend=\"the-editor\">uređivač koda</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:23 programming-reference.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands"
msgstr "Komande"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using commands you tell the turtle or &kturtle; to do something. Some "
"commands need input, some give output. <screen>\n"
"# forward is a command that needs input, in this case the number 100:\n"
"forward 100\n"
"</screen> The first line is a <link linkend=\"comment\">comment</link>. The "
"second line contains the <userinput>forward</userinput> command and the "
"<link linkend=\"number\">number</link> <userinput>100</userinput>. The "
"number is not part of command, it is considered 'input' for the command."
msgstr ""
"Korištenje komandi koje govorite kornjači ili &kturtle; da nešto uradi. Neke "
"komande trebaju ulaz, neke daju izlaz. <screen>\n"
"# naprijed je komanda koja treba ulaz, u ovom slučaju broj 100:\n"
"naprijed 100\n"
"</screen> Prvi red je <link linkend=\"comment\">komentar</link>. Drugi red "
"sadrži <userinput>forward</userinput> komandu i <link linkend=\"number"
"\">broj</link> <userinput>100</userinput>. Broj nije dio komande, on se "
"smatra 'ulazom' za komandu."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some commands like &eg; <userinput>go</userinput> need more than one input "
"value. Multiple values have to be separated using the <userinput>,</"
"userinput> character (comma)."
msgstr ""
"Neke komande kao &eg; <userinput>go</userinput> trebaju više od jedne "
"vrijednosti ulaza. Višestruke vrijednosti moraju biti odvojene korištenjem "
"<userinput>,</userinput> karaktera (zarez)."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a detailed overview of all commands that &kturtle; supports go <link "
"linkend=\"commands\">here</link>. Built-in commands are "
"<glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> in dark blue"
msgstr ""
"Za detaljan pregled svih komandi koje &kturtle; podržava idite <link linkend="
"\"commands\">ovdje</link>. Ugrađene komande su <glossterm>naglašene</"
"glossterm> tamno plavom."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numbers"
msgstr "Brojevi"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most likely you already know quite a bit about numbers. The way numbers are "
"used in &kturtle; is not much different from spoken language, or math."
msgstr ""
"Najvjerovatnije vi već znate dosta o brojevima. Način na koji se brojevi "
"koriste u &kturtle; nije puno drugačiji od govornog jezika ili matematike."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We have the so called natural numbers: <userinput>0</userinput>, "
"<userinput>1</userinput>, <userinput>2</userinput>, <userinput>3</"
"userinput>, <userinput>4</userinput>, <userinput>5</userinput>, etc. The "
"negative numbers: <userinput>-1</userinput>, <userinput>-2</userinput>, "
"<userinput>-3</userinput>, etc. And the numbers with decimals, or dot-"
"numbers, for example: <userinput>0.1</userinput>, <userinput>3.14</"
"userinput>, <userinput>33.3333</userinput>, <userinput>-5.05</userinput>, "
"<userinput>-1.0</userinput>. The <userinput>.</userinput> character (dot) is "
"used as decimal separator."
msgstr ""
"Imamo tzv. prirodne brojeve: <userinput>0</userinput>, <userinput>1</"
"userinput>, <userinput>2</userinput>, <userinput>3</userinput>, "
"<userinput>4</userinput>, <userinput>5</userinput>, itd. , negativne "
"brojeve: <userinput>-1</userinput>, <userinput>-2</userinput>, "
"<userinput>-3</userinput>, itd. i brojeve sa decimalama, ili tačka-brojevi, "
"a primjer: <userinput>0.1</userinput>, <userinput>3.14</userinput>, "
"<userinput>33.3333</userinput>, <userinput>-5.05</userinput>, "
"<userinput>-1.0</userinput>. <userinput>.</userinput> karakter (tačka) se "
"koristi za odvajanje decimala."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Numbers can be used in <link linkend=\"mathematical-operators\">mathematical "
"operators</link> and <link linkend=\"comparing-operators\">comparison "
"operators</link>. They can also be stored in <link linkend=\"assignment-of-"
"variables\">variables</link>. Numbers are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> "
"in dark red."
msgstr ""
"Brojevi se mogu koristiti u <link linkend=\"mathematical-operators"
"\">matematički operatori</link> i <link linkend=\"comparing-operators"
"\">operatori poređenja</link>. Oni takođe mogu biti pohranjeni u <link "
"linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">varijable</link>. Brojevi su "
"<glossterm>označeni</glossterm> u tamno crvenom."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strings"
msgstr "Stringovi"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First an example: <screen>\n"
"print \"Hello, I'm a string.\"\n"
"</screen> In this example <userinput>print</userinput> is a command where "
"<userinput>\"Hello, I'm a string.\"</userinput> is a string. Strings start "
"and end with the <userinput>\"</userinput> mark, by these marks &kturtle; "
"knows it is a string."
msgstr ""
"Prvo jedan primjer <screen>\n"
"štampaj \"Zdravo, ja sam string.\"\n"
"</screen> U ovom primjeru <userinput>štampaj</userinput> je komanda gdje "
"<userinput>\"Zdravo, ja sam string.\"</userinput> je string. Stringovi "
"počinju i završavaju sa <userinput>\"</userinput> oznakom, ovim oznakama "
"&kturtle; zna da je to string."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Strings can be put in <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">variables</"
"link>, just like <link linkend=\"number\">numbers</link>. Yet, unlike "
"numbers, strings cannot be used in <link linkend=\"mathematical-operators"
"\">mathematical operators</link> or <link linkend=\"comparing-operators"
"\">comparison operators</link>. Strings are <glossterm>highlighted</"
"glossterm> with red."
msgstr ""
"Stringovi mogu biti stavljeni u <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables"
"\">varijable</link>, baš kao <link linkend=\"number\">brojevi</link>. Ipak, "
"za razliku od brojeva, stringovi ne mogu biti korišteni u <link linkend="
"\"mathematical-operators\">matematičkim operatorima</link> ili <link linkend="
"\"comparing-operators\">operatorima poređenja</link>. Stringovi su "
"<glossterm>označeni</glossterm> crvenim."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "Boolean (true/false) values"
msgstr "Bulove (tačno/pogešno) vrijednosti"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are only two boolean values: <userinput>true</userinput> and "
"<userinput>false</userinput>. Sometimes they are also called: on and off, "
"yes and no, one and zero. But in &turtlescript; we call them, always, "
"<userinput>true</userinput> and <userinput>false</userinput>. Have a look at "
"this piece of &turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$a = true\n"
"</screen> If you look in the <link linkend=\"the-inspector\">inspector</"
"link> you can see that the <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables"
"\">variable</link> <userinput>$a</userinput> is set to <userinput>true</"
"userinput>, and has the boolean type."
msgstr ""
"Postoje samo dvije bulove vrijednosti: <userinput>tačno</userinput> i "
"<userinput>pogrešno</userinput>. Ponekad se zovu i: uključeno i isključeno, "
"da i ne, jedan i nula. Ali u &turtlescript; mi ih uvijek zovemo "
"<userinput>tčno</userinput> i<userinput>pogrešno</userinput>. Pogledajte "
"ovaj prmjerak &turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$a = tačno\n"
"</screen> Ako pogledate u <link linkend=\"the-inspector\">pregledač</link> "
"možete vidjeti da je<link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">varijable</"
"link> <userinput>$a</userinput>namještena na <userinput>tačno</userinput>, i "
"ima bulov tip."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Often boolean values are the result of a <link linkend=\"comparing-operators"
"\">comparison operator</link>, like in the following piece of "
"&turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$answer = 10 &gt; 3\n"
"</screen> The <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">variable</link> "
"<userinput>$answer</userinput> is set to <userinput>true</userinput> because "
"<userinput>10</userinput> is larger than <userinput>3</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Često su bulove vrijednosti rezultat <link linkend=\"comparing-operators"
"\">operatora pređenja</link>, poput sljedećeg primjerka f &turtlescript;: "
"<screen>\n"
"$answer = 10 &gt; 3\n"
"</screen> <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">varijabla</link> "
"<userinput>$answer</userinput> je namještena na <userinput>tačno</userinput> "
"jer <userinput>10</userinput> je veća od <userinput>3</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Boolean values, <userinput>true</userinput> and <userinput>false</"
"userinput>, are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with dark red."
msgstr ""
"Bulove vrijednosti, <userinput>tačno</userinput> i <userinput>pogrešno</"
"userinput>, su <glossterm>označene</glossterm> tamno crvenim."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mathematical, boolean and comparing operators"
msgstr "Matematički, bulovi i operatori poređenja"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The title of this section might sound very difficult, yet it is not as "
"difficult as it sound."
msgstr ""
"Naslov ovog odjeljka može zvučati vro teškim, mada nije težak kao što zvuči."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mathematical operators"
msgstr "Matematički operatori"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are the basic math symbols known as: add (<userinput>+</userinput>), "
"subtract (<userinput>-</userinput>), multiply (<userinput>*</userinput>), "
"divide (<userinput>/</userinput>) and power (<userinput>^</userinput>)."
msgstr ""
"Ovo su osnovni matematički simboli poznati kao: dodaj (<userinput>+</"
"userinput>), oduzmi (<userinput>-</userinput>), pomnoži (<userinput>*</"
"userinput>), podijeli (<userinput>/</userinput>) i potencija (<userinput>^</"
"userinput>)."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here a small example of the mathematical operators you can use in "
"&turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$add      = 1 + 1\n"
"$subtract = 20 - 5\n"
"$multiply = 15 * 2\n"
"$divide   = 30 / 30\n"
"$power    = 2 ^ 2\n"
"</screen> The values resulting from the mathematical operations get <link "
"linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">assigned</link> to various <link linkend="
"\"assignment-of-variables\">variables</link>. Using the <link linkend=\"the-"
"inspector\">inspector</link> you can see the values."
msgstr ""
"Ovdje je mali primjer matemetičkih operatora koje možete koristiti u "
"&turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$add      = 1 + 1\n"
"$subtract = 20 - 5\n"
"$multiply = 15 * 2\n"
"$divide   = 30 / 30\n"
"$power    = 2 ^ 2.\n"
"</screen> Rezultantne vrijednosti matematičkih operacija su <link linkend="
"\"assignment-of-variables\">dodijeljene</link> raznim <link linkend="
"\"assignment-of-variables\">varijablablama</link>. Koristeći <link linkend="
"\"the-inspector\">inspektor</link> možete vidjeti vrijednosti."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you just want a simple calculation to be done you can do something like "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"Ako samo želite da bude urađen jednostavan proračun, možete uraditi nešto "
"kao ovo:"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "print 2010-12"
msgstr "štampaj 2010-12"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now an example with parentheses: <screen>\n"
"print ( ( 20 - 5 ) * 2 / 30 ) + 1\n"
"</screen> The expressions inside parentheses will be calculated first. In "
"this example, 20-5 will be calculated, then multiplied by 2, divided by 30, "
"and then 1 is added (giving 2). Parentheses can also be used in other cases."
msgstr ""
"Sada jedan primjer sa zagradama: <screen>\n"
"štampaj ( ( 20 - 5 ) * 2 / 30 ) + 1\n"
"</screen> Izraz unutar zagrada bit će prvo izračunat . U ovom primjeru, 20-5 "
"bit će izračunato, onda pomnoženo sa 2, podijeljeno sa 30, i onda se dodaje "
"1 (što daje 2). Zagrade mogu takođe biti korištene i u drugim slučajevima."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kturtle; also has more advanced mathematical features in the form of "
"commands. Have a look at the following commands but be aware that it "
"concerns advanced operations: <link linkend=\"round\">round</link>, <link "
"linkend=\"random\">random</link>, <link linkend=\"sqrt\">sqrt</link> , <link "
"linkend=\"pi\">pi</link>, <link linkend=\"sin\">sin</link>, <link linkend="
"\"cos\">cos</link>, <link linkend=\"tan\">tan</link>, <link linkend=\"arcsin"
"\">arcsin</link>, <link linkend=\"arccos\">arccos</link>, <link linkend="
"\"arctan\">arctan</link>."
msgstr ""
"&kturtle; takođe ima više naprednih matematičkih odika u obliku komandi. "
"Pogledajte sljedeće komande ali imajte na umu da se ovo tiče naprednih "
"operacija: <link linkend=\"round\">round</link>, <link linkend=\"random"
"\">random</link>, <link linkend=\"sqrt\">sqrt</link> , <link linkend=\"pi"
"\">pi</link>, <link linkend=\"sin\">sin</link>, <link linkend=\"cos\">cos</"
"link>, <link linkend=\"tan\">tan</link>, <link linkend=\"arcsin\">arcsin</"
"link>, <link linkend=\"arccos\">arccos</link>, <link linkend=\"arctan"
"\">arctan</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Boolean (true/false) operators"
msgstr "Bulovi operatori (tačno/ogrešno)"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Where <link linkend=\"mathematical-operators\">mathematical operators</link> "
"are mainly for <link linkend=\"number\">numbers</link>, boolean operators "
"are for <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean values</link> "
"(<userinput>true</userinput> and <userinput>false</userinput>). There are "
"only three boolean operators, namely: <userinput>and</userinput>, "
"<userinput>or</userinput>, and <userinput>not</userinput>. The following "
"piece of &turtlescript; shows how to use them: <screen>\n"
"$and_1_1 = true and true    # -> true\n"
"$and_1_0 = true and false   # -> false\n"
"$and_0_1 = false and true   # -> false\n"
"$and_0_0 = false and false  # -> false\n"
"\n"
"$or_1_1 = true or true    # -> true\n"
"$or_1_0 = true or false   # -> true\n"
"$or_0_1 = false or true   # -> true\n"
"$or_0_0 = false or false  # -> false\n"
"\n"
"$not_1 = not true   # -> false\n"
"$not_0 = not false  # -> true\n"
"</screen> Using the <link linkend=\"the-inspector\">inspector</link> you can "
"see the values, yet we also supply these results as little comments at the "
"end of the lines. <userinput>and</userinput> evaluates <userinput>true</"
"userinput> only if both sides are <userinput>true</userinput>. "
"<userinput>or</userinput> evaluates <userinput>true</userinput> if either "
"side is <userinput>true</userinput>. And <userinput>not</userinput> turns a "
"<userinput>true</userinput> into <userinput>false</userinput> and a "
"<userinput>false</userinput> into <userinput>true</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Tamo gdje su<link linkend=\"mathematical-operators\">matematički operatori</"
"link> uglavnom za <link linkend=\"number\">brojeve</link>, bulovi operatori "
"su za <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulove vrijednosti</link> "
"(<userinput>tačno</userinput> i <userinput>pogrešno</userinput>). Postoje "
"samo tri bulova operatora, naime: <userinput>i</userinput>, <userinput>ili</"
"userinput>, i <userinput>ne</userinput>. Sljedeći primjerak &turtlescript; "
"pokazuje kako ih koristiti: <screen>\n"
"$and_1_1 = tačno i pogrešno    # -> true\n"
"$and_1_0 = tačno i pogrešno   # -> false\n"
"$and_0_1 = pogrešno i  tačno # -> false.\n"
"\n"
"$or_1_1 = true or true    # -> true\n"
"$or_1_0 = true or false   # -> true\n"
"$or_0_1 = false or true   # -> true\n"
"$or_0_0 = false or false  # -> false\n"
"\n"
"$not_1 = not true   # -> false\n"
"$not_0 = not false  # -> true\n"
"</screen> Koristeći <link linkend=\"the-inspector\">inspektor</link> možete "
"vidjeti vrijednosti ali i dati rezultate kao male komentare na kraju "
"linijama.  <userinput>and</userinput> je <userinput>tačno</userinput> samo "
"ako su obije strane <userinput>tačno</userinput>. <userinput>ili</userinput> "
"ima vrijednost<userinput>tačno</userinput> ako je bilo koja strana "
"<userinput>tačno</userinput>. A <userinput>ne</userinput> pretvara "
"<userinput>tačno</userinput> u <userinput>netačno</userinput>  a "
"<userinput>netačno</userinput> u <userinput>tačno</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Boolean operators are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with pink."
msgstr "Bulovi operatori su <glossterm>označeni</glossterm> ružičastim."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some more advanced examples"
msgstr "Neki napredniji primjeri"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Consider the following example with <userinput>and</userinput>: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"if (($a &lt; 10) and ($b == 5)) and ($a &lt; $b) {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> In this piece of &turtlescript; the result of three <link linkend="
"\"comparing-operators\">comparing operators</link> are merged using "
"<userinput>and</userinput> operators. This means that all three have to "
"evaluate \"true\" in order for the \"hello\" to be printed."
msgstr ""
"Razmotrite sljedeći primjer sa <userinput>i</userinput>: <screen>\n"
"$a = 1\n"
"$b = 5\n"
"ako (($a &lt; 10) i ($b == 5)) i ($a &lt; $b) {\n"
"  štampaj \"zdravo\"\n"
"}. </screen>U ovom dijelu &turtlescript; rezultat tri <link linkend="
"\"comparing-operators\">operatora poređenja</link> se spaja koristeći "
"<userinput>i</userinput> operatore. To znači da sva tri moraju biti \"tačno"
"\" da bi se \"zdravo\" prikazalo."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An example with <userinput>or</userinput>: <screen>\n"
"$n = 1\n"
"if ($n &lt; 10) or ($n == 2) {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> In this piece of &turtlescript; the left side of the "
"<userinput>or</userinput> is evaluating to 'true', the right side to "
"'false'. Since one of the two sides of the <userinput>or</userinput> "
"operator is 'true', the <userinput>or</userinput> operator evaluates 'true'. "
"That means \"hello\" gets printed."
msgstr ""
"Primjer sa <userinput>ili</userinput>: <screen>\n"
"$n = 1\n"
"ako ($n &lt; 10) ili ($n == 2) {\n"
"  štampaj \"zdravo\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> U ovom primjerku &turtlescript; lijeva strana <userinput>ili</"
"userinput> je ocijenjena kao 'tačno', desna strana kao 'pogrešno'. Pošto je "
"jedna od dvije strane <userinput>ili </userinput> operatora 'tačno', "
"<userinput>ili</userinput> operator se ojenjuje kao 'tačno'. To znači da će "
"\"zdravo\" biti odštampano."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And finally an example with <userinput>not</userinput> which changes 'true' "
"into 'false' and 'false' into 'true'. Have a look:"
msgstr ""
"I konačno jedan primjer sa <userinput>ne</userinput> koji mijenja 'tačno' u "
"'pogrešno' i 'pogrešno' u 'tačno'. Pogledajte::"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$n = 1\n"
"if not ($n == 3) {\n"
"  print \"hello\"\n"
"} else {\n"
"  print \"not hello ;-)\"\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"$n = 1\n"
"ako ne ($n == 3) {\n"
"  štampaj \"zdravo\"\n"
"} inače {\n"
"  štampaj \"ne zdravo ;-)\"\n"
"}"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comparing operators"
msgstr "Operatori koji porede"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Consider this simple comparison: <screen>\n"
"$answer = 10 &gt; 3\n"
"</screen> Here <userinput>10</userinput> is compared to <userinput>3</"
"userinput> with the 'greater than' operator. The result of this comparison, "
"the <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean value</link> <userinput>true</"
"userinput> is stored in the <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables"
"\">variable</link> <userinput>$answer</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Razmotrite ovo jednostavno poređenje <screen>\n"
"$answer = 10 &gt; 3\n"
"</screen> Ovdje <userinput>10</userinput> se poredi sa <userinput>3</"
"userinput> 'veće od' operatorom. Rezultat ovog poređenja <link linkend="
"\"boolean-value\">bulova vrijednost</link> <userinput>true</userinput> je "
"pohranjena u <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">varijablama</link> "
"<userinput>$answer</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All <link linkend=\"number\">numbers</link> and <link linkend=\"assignment-"
"of-variables\">variables</link> (that contain numbers) can be compared to "
"each other with comparing operators."
msgstr ""
"Svi <link linkend=\"number\">brojevi</link> i <link linkend=\"assignment-of-"
"variables\">varijable</link> (koje sadrže brojeve) mogu se porediti jedna sa "
"drugom sa operatorima poređenja."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here are all possible comparing operators: <table> <title>Types of "
"questions</title> <tgroup cols=\"3\"> <tbody> <row> <entry><userinput>$A == "
"$B</userinput></entry> <entry>equals</entry> <entry>answer is <quote>true</"
"quote> if <userinput>$A</userinput> equals <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> "
"</row> <row> <entry><userinput>$A != $B</userinput></entry> <entry>not-"
"equals</entry> <entry>answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>$A</"
"userinput> does not equal <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </row> <row> "
"<entry><userinput>$A &gt; $B</userinput></entry> <entry>greater than</entry> "
"<entry>answer is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>$A</userinput> is greater "
"than <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </row> <row> <entry><userinput>$A "
"&lt; $B</userinput></entry> <entry>smaller than</entry> <entry>answer is "
"<quote>true</quote> if <userinput>$A</userinput> is smaller than <userinput>"
"$B</userinput></entry> </row> <row> <entry><userinput>$A &gt;= $B</"
"userinput></entry> <entry>greater than or equals</entry> <entry>answer is "
"<quote>true</quote> if <userinput>$A</userinput> is greater than or equals "
"<userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </row> <row> <entry><userinput>$A &lt;= "
"$B</userinput></entry> <entry>smaller than or equals</entry> <entry>answer "
"is <quote>true</quote> if <userinput>$A</userinput> is smaller than or "
"equals <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </row> </tbody> </tgroup> </table> "
"Please note that $A and $B have to be <link linkend=\"number\">numbers</"
"link> or <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">variables</link> that "
"contain numbers."
msgstr ""
"Ovdje su svi mogući operatori poređenja: <table> <title>Tipovi pitanja</"
"title> <tgroup cols=\"3\"> <tbody> <row> <entry><userinput>$A == $B</"
"userinput></entry> <entry>jednako je</entry> <entry>odgovor je <quote>tačan</"
"quote> ukoliko <userinput>$A</userinput> je jednak <userinput>$B</"
"userinput></entry> </row> <row> <entry><userinput>$A != $B</userinput></"
"entry> <entry>nije jednako</entry> <entry>odgovor je <quote>tačan</quote> "
"ukoliko <userinput>$A</userinput> nije jednako <userinput>$B</userinput></"
"entry> </row> <row> <entry><userinput>$A &gt; $B</userinput></entry> "
"<entry>veće od</entry> <entry>odgovor je <quote>tačan</quote> ukoliko "
"<userinput>$A</userinput> je veći od <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </"
"row> <row> <entry><userinput>$A &lt; $B</userinput></entry> <entry>manji od</"
"entry> <entry>odgovor je <quote>tačan</quote> ukoliko <userinput>$A</"
"userinput> je manje od <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </row> <row> "
"<entry><userinput>$A &gt;= $B</userinput></entry> <entry>veće od ili je "
"jednako </entry> <entry>odgovor je <quote>tačan</quote> ukoliko <userinput>"
"$A</userinput> je veće ili jednako <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </row> "
"<row> <entry><userinput>$A &lt;= $B</userinput></entry> <entry>manje ili "
"jednako</entry> <entry>odgovor je <quote>tačan</quote>ukoliko <userinput>$A</"
"userinput> je manji ili jednak <userinput>$B</userinput></entry> </row> </"
"tbody> </tgroup> </table> Molimo da primijetite da $A i $B moraju biti <link "
"linkend=\"number\">brojevi</link> ili <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables"
"\">varijable</link> koje sadrže brojeve."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using commands you tell the turtle or &kturtle; to do something. Some "
"commands need input, some give output. In this section we explain all the "
"built-in commands of &kturtle;. Alternatively, using <link linkend=\"learn"
"\">learn</link>, you can create your own commands. Built-in commands we "
"discuss here are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with dark blue."
msgstr ""
"Korištenjem komandi vi kažete kornjači ili &kturtle; da nešto uradi. Neke "
"komande trebaju ulaz, nke daju izlaz.U ovom odjeljku mi objašnjavamo sve "
"ugrađene komande &kturtle;. Alternativno, korištenjem <link linkend=\"learn"
"\">učenja</link>, možete stvoriti vaše vlastite komande. O ugrađenim "
"komandama mi pričamo kao o ovdje <glossterm>označenim</glossterm> tamno "
"plavim."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving the turtle"
msgstr "Pomjeranje kornjače"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are several commands to move the turtle over the screen."
msgstr "Postoji nekoliko komandi kako bi pomjerali kornjaču po ekranu."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>forward (fw)</term>"
msgstr "<term>naprijed (fw)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>forward (fw)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>naprijed (fw)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "forward X"
msgstr "naprijed X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>forward</userinput> moves the turtle forward by the amount of X "
"pixels. When the pen is down the turtle will leave a trail. "
"<userinput>forward</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>fw</"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>naprijed</userinput> pomjera kornjaču za iznos X pikselas. Kada "
"je pero spušteno kornjača će ostaviti trag. <userinput>naprijed</userinput> "
"može biti skraćena na <userinput>fw</userinput>"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>backward (bw)</term>"
msgstr "<term>natrag (bw)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>backward (bw)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>natrag (bw)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "backward X"
msgstr "natrag X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>backward</userinput> moves the turtle backward by the amount of X "
"pixels. When the pen is down the turtle will leave a trail. "
"<userinput>backward</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>bw</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>natrag</userinput> pomjera kornjaču natrag za iznos X piksela. "
"Kada je pero spušteno kornjača će ostaviti trag. <userinput>natrag</"
"userinput> može bit skraćeno na <userinput>bw</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>turnleft (tl)</term>"
msgstr "<term>skrenilijevo (tl)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>turnleft (tl)</primary>"
msgstr "<term>skrenilijevo (tl)</term>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "turnleft X"
msgstr "skrenilijevo X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>turnleft</userinput> commands the turtle to turn an amount of X "
"degrees to the left. <userinput>turnleft</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>tl</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>skrenilijevo</userinput>daje naredbu kornjači da skrene za iznos "
"stepeni X ulijevo. <userinput>skrenilijevo</userinput> može biti skraćen na "
"<userinput>tl</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>turnright (tr)</term>"
msgstr "<term>skrenidesno (tr)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>turnright (tr)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>skrenidesno (tr)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "turnright X"
msgstr "skrenidesno X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>turnright</userinput> the turtle to turn an amount of X degrees "
"to the right. <userinput>turnright</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>tr</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>skrenidesno</userinput> daje naredbu kornjači da skrene za iznos "
"stepeni X udesno. <userinput>skrenidesno</userinput> može se skratiti na "
"<userinput>tr</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>direction (dir)</term>"
msgstr "<term>smjer (dir)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>direction (dir)</primary>"
msgstr "<term>smjer (dir)</term>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "direction X"
msgstr "smjer X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>direction</userinput> set the turtle's direction to an amount of "
"X degrees counting from zero, and thus is not relative to the turtle's "
"previous direction. <userinput>direction</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>dir</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>smjer</userinput> namješta smjer kornjače na iznos stepeni X "
"mjereno od nule, i prema tome nije relativno u odnosu na kornjačin raniji "
"smjer. <userinput>smjer</userinput> može bit skraćen na<userinput>dir</"
"userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>getdirection</term>"
msgstr "<term>uzmismjer</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>getdirection</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>uzmismjer</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>getdirection</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>uzmismjer</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>getdirection</userinput> returns the turtle's direction as an "
"amount of degrees counting from zero, where zero is the direction when the "
"turtle is pointing upwards."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>uzmismjer</userinput> vraća smjer kornjače kao iznos stepeni "
"brojeći od nule, gdje je nula smjer kada kornjača pokazuje nagore."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>center</term>"
msgstr "<term>centar</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>center</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>centar</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>center</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>centar</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>center</userinput> moves the turtle to the center on the canvas."
msgstr "<userinput>centar</userinput> pomjera kornjaču prema centru platna."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>go</term>"
msgstr "<term>idi</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>go</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>idi</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "go X,Y"
msgstr "idi X,Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>go</userinput> commands the turtle to go to a certain place on "
"the canvas. This place is X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm> "
"from the left of the canvas, and Y <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</"
"glossterm> from the top of the canvas."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>idi</userinput> daje naredbu kornjači da ide na određeno mjesto "
"na platnu. Ovo mjesto je X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">piksela</glossterm> "
"od lijeve strane platna , i Y <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</"
"glossterm> od vrha platna."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>gox</term>"
msgstr "<term>idix</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "gox (gx)"
msgstr "idix (gx)"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "gox X"
msgstr "idix X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gox</userinput> using this command the turtle will move to X "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm> from the left of the canvas "
"whilst staying at the same height. <userinput>gox</userinput> can be "
"abbreviated to <userinput>gx</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>idix</userinput> korištenjem ove komande kornjaća će se pomjeriti "
"na X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">piksela</glossterm> od lijeve strane "
"platna ostajući na istoj visini. <userinput>idix</userinput> može biti "
"skraćeno na <userinput>gx</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>goy</term>"
msgstr "<term>idiy</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "goy (gy)"
msgstr "idiy (gy)"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "goy Y"
msgstr "idiy Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>goy</userinput> using this command the turtle will move to Y "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm> from the top of the canvas "
"whilst staying at the same distance from the left border of the canvas. "
"<userinput>goy</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>gy</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>idiy</userinput> korištenjem ove komande kornjača će se pomjeriti "
"na Y <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">piksela</glossterm> od vrha platna "
"ostajući na istoj udaljenosti od lijeve ivice platna. <userinput>idiy</"
"userinput> može biti skraćeno na <userinput>gy</userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the commands <userinput>go</userinput>, <userinput>gox</userinput>, "
"<userinput>goy</userinput> and <userinput>center</userinput> the turtle will "
"not draw a line, no matter if the pen is up or down."
msgstr ""
"Korištenjem komandi <userinput>idi</userinput>, <userinput>idix</userinput>, "
"<userinput>idiy</userinput> i <userinput>centar</userinput> kornjača neće "
"crtati liniju, bez obzira je li pero podignuto ili spušteno."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where is the turtle?"
msgstr "Gdje je kornjača?"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two commands which return the position of the turtle on the screen."
msgstr "Postoje dvije komande koje vraćaju poziciju kornjače na ekranu."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>getx</term>"
msgstr "<term>uzmix</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>getx</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>uzmix</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>getx</userinput> returns the number of pixels from the left of "
"the canvas to the current position of the turtle."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>uzmix</userinput> vraća broj piksela s lijeve strane platna "
"trenutnoj poziciji kornjače."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>gety</term>"
msgstr "<term>uzmiy</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>gety</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>uzmiy</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gety</userinput> returns the number of pixels from the top of the "
"canvas to the current position of the turtle."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>uzmiy</userinput> vraća broj piksela sod vrha platna trenutnoj "
"poziciji kornjače."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "The turtle has a pen"
msgstr "Kornjača ima pero"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The turtle has a pen that draws a line when the turtle moves. There are a "
"few commands to control the pen. In this section we explain these commands."
msgstr ""
"Kornjača ima pero koje rta liniju kad se kornjača kreće. Postoji nekoliko "
"komandi da se upravlja perom. U ovom odjeljku mi objašnjavamo ove komande."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>penup (pu)</term>"
msgstr "<term>perogore (pu)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>penup (pu)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>pergore (pu)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "penup"
msgstr "perogore"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>penup</userinput> lifts the pen from the canvas. When the pen is "
"<quote>up</quote> no line will be drawn when the turtle moves. See also "
"<userinput>pendown</userinput>. <userinput>penup</userinput> can be "
"abbreviated to <userinput>pu</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>perogore</userinput> podiže pero sa platna. Kada je pero "
"<quote>podignuto</quote> nikakva linija se neće crtati kad se kornjača "
"kreće. Pogledajte takođe <userinput>perodolje</userinput>. "
"<userinput>perogore</userinput> može biti skraćeno na <userinput>pu</"
"userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>pendown (pd)</term>"
msgstr "<term>perodolje (pd)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>pendown (pd)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>perodolje (pd)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "pendown"
msgstr "perodolje"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>pendown</userinput> presses the pen down on the canvas. When the "
"pen is press <quote>down</quote> on the canvas a line will be drawn when the "
"turtle moves. See also <userinput>penup</userinput>. <userinput>pendown</"
"userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>pd</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>perodolje</userinput> pritišće pero na platno. Kad je pero "
"pritisnuto <quote>dolje</quote> na platno crtaće se linija kad se kornjača "
"kreće. Pogledajte takođe <userinput>perogore</userinput>. "
"<userinput>perodolje</userinput> može biti skraćeno na <userinput>pd</"
"userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>penwidth (pw)</term>"
msgstr "<term>peroširina (pw)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>penwidth (pw)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>peroširina (pw)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid "penwidth X"
msgstr "peroširina X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>penwidth</userinput> sets the width of the pen (the line width) "
"to an amount of X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>. "
"<userinput>penwidth</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>pw</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>peroširina</userinput> namješta širinu pera (širinu linije) na "
"iznos od X <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">piksela</glossterm>. "
"<userinput>peroirina</userinput> može bit skraćeno na <userinput>pw</"
"userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>pencolor (pc)</term>"
msgstr "<term>peroboja (pc)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>pencolor (pc)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>peroboja (pc)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "pencolor R,G,B"
msgstr "peroboja R,G,B"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>pencolor</userinput> sets the color of the pen. "
"<userinput>pencolor</userinput> takes an <glossterm linkend=\"rgb\">RGB "
"combination</glossterm> as input. <userinput>pencolor</userinput> can be "
"abbreviated to <userinput>pc</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>peroboja</userinput> namješta boju pera. <userinput>peroboja</"
"userinput> uzima jednu <glossterm linkend=\"rgb\">RGB kobinaciju</glossterm> "
"kao ulaz. <userinput>peroboja</userinput> može biti skraćena na "
"<userinput>pc</userinput>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands to control the canvas"
msgstr "Komande za upravljanje platnom"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are several commands to control the canvas."
msgstr "Postoji nekoliko komandi za upravljanje platnom."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>canvassize (cs)</term>"
msgstr "<term>veličinaplatna (cs)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>canvassize (cs)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>veličinaplatna (cs)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid "canvassize X,Y"
msgstr "veličinaplatna X,Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the <userinput>canvassize</userinput> command you can set the size of "
"the canvas. It takes X and Y as input, where X is the new canvas width in "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>, and Y is the new height of "
"the canvas in <glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>. "
"<userinput>canvassize</userinput> can be abbreviated to <userinput>cs</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""
"Sa <userinput>veličinaplatna</userinput> komandom možete namještati veličinu "
"platna. Traba vam X i Y kao ulaz, gdje je X nova širina platna u <glossterm "
"linkend=\"pixels\">pikselima</glossterm>, i Y je nova visin platna u "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pikselima</glossterm>. "
"<userinput>veličinaplatna</userinput> može biti skraćena na<userinput>cs</"
"userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>canvascolor (cc)</term>"
msgstr "<term>bojaplatna (cc)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>canvascolor (cc)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>bojaplatna (cc)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "canvascolor R,G,B"
msgstr "bojaplatna R,G,B"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>canvascolor</userinput> set the color of the canvas. "
"<userinput>canvascolor</userinput> takes an <glossterm linkend=\"rgb\">RGB "
"combination</glossterm> as input. <userinput>canvascolor</userinput> can be "
"abbreviated to <userinput>cc</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>bojaplatna</userinput> namješta boju platna. "
"<userinput>bojaplatna</userinput> uzima jednu <glossterm linkend=\"rgb\">RGB "
"kombinaciju</glossterm> kao ulaz. <userinput>bojaplatna</userinput> može "
"biti skraćena na <userinput>cc</userinput>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands to clean up"
msgstr "Komande za čišćenje"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two commands to clean up the canvas after you have made a mess."
msgstr ""
"Postoje dvije komande da se očisti platno nakon što ste napravili nered."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>clear (ccl)</term>"
msgstr "<term>očisti (ccl)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>clear (ccl)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>očisti (ccl)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "clear"
msgstr "očisti"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With <userinput>clear</userinput> you can clean all drawings from the "
"canvas. All other things remain: the position and angle of the turtle, the "
"canvascolor, the visibility of the turtle, and the canvas size."
msgstr ""
"Sa <userinput>očisti</userinput> možete očistiti sve crteže sa platna. Sve "
"druge stvari ostaju: položaj i ugao kornjače, bojaplatna, vidljivost "
"kornjače, i veličina platna."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>reset</term>"
msgstr "<term>resetuj</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>reset</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>resetuj</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>reset</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>resetuj</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>reset</userinput> cleans much more thoroughly than the "
"<userinput>clear</userinput> command. After a <userinput>reset</userinput> "
"command everything is like is was when you had just started &kturtle;. The "
"turtle is positioned at the middle of the screen, the canvas color is white, "
"the turtle draws a black line on the canvas and the canvassize is set to 400 "
"x 400 pixels."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>resetuj</userinput> čisti puno temeljitije od <userinput>očisti</"
"userinput> komande. Nakon <userinput>resetuj</userinput> komande sve je kao "
"što je bilo kad ste tek započeli &kturtle;. Kornjača je smještena na sredinu "
"ekrana, boja platna je bijela, kornjača crta crnu liniju na platnu i "
"veličina platna je namještena na 400 x 400 piksela."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "The turtle is a sprite"
msgstr "Kornjača je duh -vilenjak"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First a brief explanation of what sprites are: sprites are small pictures "
"that can be moved around the screen, like we often see in computer games. "
"Our turtle is also a sprite. For more info see the glossary on <glossterm "
"linkend=\"sprites\">sprites</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"Najrije kratko objašnjenje šta su duhovi: duhovi su male slike koje se mogu "
"pomjerati po ekranu, kao što često vidimo u računarskim igricama. Naša "
"kornjača je takođe duh. Za više infrmacija pogledajte riječnik na <glossterm "
"linkend=\"sprites\">sprites</glossterm>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next you will find a full overview on all commands to work with sprites."
msgstr "Sljedeće ćete naći potpuni pregled svih komandi da radite sa duhovima."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[The current version of &kturtle; does not yet support the use of sprites "
"other than the turtle. With future versions you will be able to change the "
"turtle into something of your own design]"
msgstr ""
"[Trenutna verzija &kturtle; još ne podržava korištenje duhova osim kornjače. "
"Sa budućim verzijama moći ćete mijenjati kornjaču u nešto vašeg vlastitog "
"dizajna]"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>spriteshow (ss)</term>"
msgstr "<term>prikazduha (ss)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>spriteshow (ss)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>prikazduha (ss)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "spriteshow"
msgstr "prikazduha"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>spriteshow</userinput> makes the turtle visible again after it "
"has been hidden. <userinput>spriteshow</userinput> can be abbreviated to "
"<userinput>ss</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>prikazduha</userinput> čini vašu kornjaču vidljivom nakon što je "
"bil nevidjiva. <userinput>prikazduha</userinput> može biti skračen na "
"<userinput>ss</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>spritehide (sh)</term>"
msgstr "<term>sakrivanjeduha (sh)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>spritehide (sh)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>sakrivanjeduha (sh)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "spritehide"
msgstr "sakrivanjeduha"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>spritehide</userinput> hides the turtle. This can be used if the "
"turtle does not fit in your drawing. <userinput>spritehide</userinput> can "
"be abbreviated to <userinput>sh</userinput>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sakrivanjeduha</userinput> sakriva kornjaču. Ovo može biti "
"korisno ukoliko kornjača ne može stati u vaš crtež. "
"<userinput>sakrivanjeduha</userinput> može biti skračeno na<userinput>sh</"
"userinput>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can the turtle write?"
msgstr "Može i kornjača pisati?"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The answer is: <quote>yes</quote>. The turtle can write: it writes just "
"about everything you command it to."
msgstr ""
"Odovor je: <quote>da</quote>. Kornjača može pisati: ona piše štogod joj vi "
"naredili."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>print</term>"
msgstr "<term>odštampaj</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>print</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>odštampaj</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "print X"
msgstr "odštampaj X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>print</userinput> command is used to command the turtle to "
"write something on the canvas. <userinput>print</userinput> takes numbers "
"and strings as input. You can <userinput>print</userinput> various numbers "
"and strings using the <quote>+</quote> symbol. See here a small example:"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>odštampaj</userinput> komanda se koristi za naređivanje konjači "
"da nešto napiše na platnu. <userinput>odštamaj</userinput> prima brojeve i "
"stingove kao ulazne informacije. Možete <userinput>odštampaj</userinput> "
"razne brojeve i stringove koristeći <quote>+</quote> simbol. Ovo je mali "
"primjer:"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$year = 2003\n"
"$author = \"Cies\"\n"
"print $author + \" started the KTurtle project in \" + $year + \" and still "
"enjoys working on it!\""
msgstr ""
"$year = 2003\n"
"$author = \"Cies\"\n"
"odštampaj $author + \" started the KTurtle project in \" + $year + \" and "
"still enjoys working on it!\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>fontsize</term>"
msgstr "<term>veličinafonta</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>fontsize</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>veličinafonta</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "fontsize X"
msgstr "veličinafonta X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>fontsize</userinput> sets the size of the font that is used by "
"<userinput>print</userinput>. <userinput>fontsize</userinput> takes one "
"input which should be a number. The size is set in <glossterm linkend="
"\"pixels\">pixels</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>veličinafonta</userinput> spodešava veličinu fonta koji koristi "
"<userinput>odštampaj</userinput>. <userinput>veličinafonta</userinput> na "
"ulazu prima argument koji bi trebao biti broj. Veličina se podešava u "
"<glossterm linkend=\"pixels\">pikselima</glossterm>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mathematical commands"
msgstr "Matematičke komande"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following commands are &kturtle;'s more advanced mathematical commands."
msgstr "Slijedeće komande su &kturtle; naprednije matematičke komande."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>round</term>"
msgstr "<term>cjelobrojnavrijednost</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>round</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>cjelobrojnavrijednost</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid "round(x)"
msgstr "cjelobrojnavrijednost(x)"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>round</userinput> the given number to the nearest integer. "
"<screen>\n"
"print round(10.8)\n"
"forward 20\n"
"print round(10.3)\n"
"</screen> With this code the turtle will print the numbers 11 and 10."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cjelobrojnavrijednost</userinput> najbliža cjelobrojna "
"vrijednost. <screen>\n"
"odštampaj cjelobrojnavrijednost(10.8)\n"
"naprijed 20\n"
"odštampaj cjelobrojnavrijednost(10.3)\n"
"</screen> Sa ovim kodom vaše će kornjača odštampati brojeve 11 i 10."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>random (rnd)</term>"
msgstr "<term>nasumično(rnd)</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>random (rnd)</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>nasumično (rnd)</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "random X,Y"
msgstr "nasumično X,Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>random</userinput> is a command that takes input and gives "
"output. As input are required two numbers, the first (X) sets the minimum "
"output, the second (Y) sets the maximum. The output is a randomly chosen "
"number that is equal or greater than the minimum and equal or smaller than "
"the maximum. Here a small example: <screen>\n"
"repeat 500 {\n"
"  $x = random 1,20\n"
"  forward $x\n"
"  turnleft 10 - $x\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Using the <userinput>random</userinput> command you can add a bit "
"of chaos to your program."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>nasumično</userinput> je komanda koja prima informacije i daje "
"informacije. Kao ulaz zahtijeva dva broja, prvi (X) podešava minimalni "
"izlaz, a druga (Y) maksimalni. Izlaz je nasumično odabran broj koji je "
"jednak ili veći od minimuma ili jednak ili manji od maksimuma. Evo malog "
"primjera: <screen>\n"
"ponovi 500 {\n"
"  $x = nasumično 1,20\n"
" naprijed $x\n"
" lijevo 10 - $x\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Koristeći <userinput>nasumično</userinput> komandu možete dodati "
"malo haosa u vaš program."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>mod</term>"
msgstr "<term>ostatak</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>mod</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>ostatak</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid "mod X,Y"
msgstr "ostatak X,Y"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>mod</userinput> returns remainder of the division of first "
"number by the second number."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ostatak</userinput> vraća ostatak dijeljenja prvog broja drugim "
"brojem."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>sqrt</term>"
msgstr "<term> korijen </term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>sqrt</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>korijen</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid "sqrt X"
msgstr "korijen iz X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>sqrt</userinput> command is sued to find the square root of a "
"number, X."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>korijen</userinput> komanda se koristi nađe kvadratni korijen "
"broja X."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>pi</term>"
msgstr "<term>pi</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>pi</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>pi</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>pi</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>pi</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid "This command returns the constant Pi, <userinput>3.14159</userinput>."
msgstr "Ova komanda vraća konstantu Pi, <userinput>3.14159</userinput>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"sin<indexterm><primary>sin</primary></indexterm>, "
"cos<indexterm><primary>cos</primary></indexterm>, tan"
msgstr ""
"sin<indexterm><primary>sin</primary></indexterm>, "
"cos<indexterm><primary>cos</primary></indexterm>, tan"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>tan</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>tan</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"sin X\n"
"cos X\n"
"tan X"
msgstr ""
"sin X\n"
"cos X\n"
"tan X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These three commands represent the world famous trigoniometrical functions "
"<userinput>sin</userinput>, <userinput>cos</userinput> and <userinput>tan</"
"userinput>. The input argument of these commands, X, is a <link linkend="
"\"number\">number</link>."
msgstr ""
"Ove tri komande predstavljaju svjetski poznate trigonometrijske funkcije "
"<userinput>sin</userinput>, <userinput>cos</userinput> i <userinput>tan</"
"userinput>. Ulazni argument ovih komandi, X, je <link linkend=\"number"
"\">broj</link>."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"arcsin<indexterm><primary>arcsin</primary></indexterm>, "
"arccos<indexterm><primary>arccos</primary></indexterm>, arctan"
msgstr ""
"arcsin<indexterm><primary>arcsin</primary></indexterm>, "
"arccos<indexterm><primary>arccos</primary></indexterm>, arctan"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "arctan"
msgstr "arctan"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"arcsin X\n"
"arccos X\n"
"arctan X"
msgstr ""
"arcsin X\n"
"arccos X\n"
"arctan X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These commands are the inverse functions of <link linkend=\"sin\">sin</"
"link>, <link linkend=\"cos\">cos</link> and <link linkend=\"tan\">tan</"
"link>. The input argument of these commands, X, is a <link linkend=\"number"
"\">number</link>."
msgstr ""
"Ove komande su inverzne funkcije <link linkend=\"sin\">sin</link>, <link "
"linkend=\"cos\">cos</link> i <link linkend=\"tan\">tan</link>. Ulazni "
"argument ovih komandi, X, je <link linkend=\"number\">broj</link>."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input and feedback through dialogs"
msgstr "Ulaz i povratne informacije kroz dijaloge"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A dialog is a small pop-up window that provides some feedback or asks for "
"some input. &kturtle; has two commands for dialogs, namely: "
"<userinput>message</userinput> and <userinput>ask</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"Dijalog je mali prozor koji iskače a pruža neke povratne informacije ili "
"traži neki ulaz. &kturtle; ima dvije komande za dijaloge, naime: "
"<userinput>poruka</userinput> i <userinput>traži</userinput>"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>message</term>"
msgstr "<term>poruka</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>message</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>poruka</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid "message X"
msgstr "poruka X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>message</userinput> command takes a <link linkend=\"string"
"\">string</link> as input. It shows a pop-up dialog containing the text from "
"the <link linkend=\"string\">string</link>."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>poruka</userinput> komanda uzima <link linkend=\"string\">string</"
"link> kao ulaz. Ona pokazuje dijalog koji iskače a sadrži tekst iz <link "
"linkend=\"string\">stringa</link>."

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"message \"Cies started KTurtle in 2003 and still enjoys working on it!\""
msgstr ""
"poruka \"Cies je započeo KTurtle 2003. i još uvijek uživa radeći na njemu!\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>ask</term>"
msgstr "<term>traži</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>ask</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>traži</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "ask X"
msgstr "traži X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>ask</userinput> takes a <link linkend=\"string\">string</link> as "
"input. It shows this string in a pop-up dialog (similar to <link linkend="
"\"message\">message</link>), along with an input field. After the user has "
"entered a <link linkend=\"number\">number</link> or a <link linkend=\"string"
"\">string</link> into this, the result can be stored in a <link linkend="
"\"assignment-of-variables\">variable</link> or passed as an argument to a "
"<link linkend=\"commands\">command</link>. For example: <screen>\n"
"$in = ask \"What is your year of birth?\"\n"
"$out = 2003 - $in\n"
"print \"In 2003 you were \" + $out + \" years old at some point.\"\n"
"</screen> If the user cancels the input dialog, or does not enter anything "
"at all, the <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">variable</link> is "
"empty."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>traži</userinput> uzima jedan <link linkend=\"string\">string</"
"link> kao ulaz. On pokazuje ovaj string u iskačućem dijalogu(slično kao "
"<link linkend=\"message\">poruka</link>), zajedno sa ulaznim poljem. Nakon "
"što je korisnik ušao u <link linkend=\"number\">broj</link> ili <link "
"linkend=\"string\">string</link> u ovom, rezultat može biti pohranjen u "
"<link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">promjenjive</link> ili proslijeđen "
"kao argument u <link linkend=\"commands\">komande</link>. Na primjer: "
"<screen>\n"
"$in = traži \"What is your year of birth?\"\n"
"$out = 2003 - $in\n"
"štampaj \"In 2003 you were \" + $out + \" years old at some point.\"\n"
"</screen> Ukoliko korisnik otkaže ulazni dijalog, ili ne unese baš ništa, "
"<link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">promjenljiva</link> je prazna."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "Assignment of variables"
msgstr "Dodjeljivanje promjenljivih"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First we have a look at variables, then we look at assigning values to those "
"variables."
msgstr ""
"Prvo moramo da pogledamo promjenljive, onda posmatramo dodjeljivanje "
"vrijednosti tim promjenljivim."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Variables are words that start with a <quote>$</quote>, in the <link linkend="
"\"the-editor\">editor</link> they are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> "
"with purple."
msgstr ""
"Promjenljive su riječi koje počinju sa <quote>$</quote>, u <link linkend="
"\"the-editor\">uređivač</link> oni su <glossterm>označeni</glossterm> "
"ljubičastim."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Variables can contain any <link linkend=\"number\">number</link>, <link "
"linkend=\"string\">string</link> or <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean "
"(true/false) value</link>. Using the assignment, <userinput>=</userinput>, a "
"variable is given its content. It will keep that content until the program "
"finishes executing or until the variable is reassigned to something else."
msgstr ""
"Promjenljive mogu sadržavati bilo kakav <link linkend=\"number\">broj</"
"link>, <link linkend=\"string\">string</link> ili <link linkend=\"boolean-"
"value\">bulovu (tačno/pogrešno) vrijednost</link>. Koristeći dodjeljivanje, "
"<userinput>=</userinput>, promjenljivoj se daje njen sadržaj. Ona će "
"zadržati taj sadržaj dok program ne završi izvršenje ili dok se promjenljiva "
"ne dodijeli nečem drugom."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use variables, once assigned, just as if they are their content. For "
"instance in the following piece of &turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$x = 10\n"
"$x = $x / 3\n"
"print $x\n"
"</screen> First the variable <userinput>$x</userinput> is assigned to "
"<userinput>10</userinput>. Then <userinput>$x</userinput> is reassigned to "
"itself divided by <userinput>3</userinput> &mdash; this effectively means "
"<userinput>$x</userinput> is reassigned to product of <userinput>10 / 3</"
"userinput>. Finally <userinput>$x</userinput> is printed. In line two and "
"three you see that <userinput>$x</userinput> is used as if it is its "
"contents."
msgstr ""
"Možete koristiti promjenljive, jednom dodijeljene, samo kao da su svoj "
"sadržaj. Na primjer u sljedećem dijelu &turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$x = 10\n"
"$x = $x / 3\n"
"štampaj $x\n"
"</screen> Prvo je promjenljiva <userinput>$x</userinput> dodijeljena "
"<userinput>10</userinput>. Onda <userinput>$x</userinput> se ponovo dodjeli "
"sebi podijeljenoj sa <userinput>3</userinput> &mdash; ovo efektivno znači "
"<userinput>$x</userinput> je ponovo dodijeljeno proizvodu <userinput>10 / 3</"
"userinput>. Konačno <userinput>$x</userinput> je štampan. U drugom i trećem "
"redu vidite da <userinput>$x</userinput> se koristi kao da je svoj sadržaj."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Variables have to be assigned in order to be used. For example: <screen>\n"
"print $n\n"
"</screen> Will result in an error message."
msgstr ""
"Promjenljive moraju biti dodijeljene da bi se koristile. Na primjer: "
"<screen>\n"
"štampaj $n\n"
"</screen> će kao rezultat imati poruku o grešci."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please consider the following piece of &turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$a = 2004\n"
"$b = 25\n"
"\n"
"# the next command prints \"2029\"\n"
"print $a + $b\n"
"backward 30\n"
"# the next command prints \"2004 plus 25 equals 2029\"\n"
"print $a + \" plus \" + $b + \" equals \" + ($a + $b)\n"
"</screen> In the first two lines the variables <userinput>$a</userinput> and "
"<userinput>$b</userinput> are set to 2004 and 25. Then in two "
"<userinput>print</userinput> commands with a <userinput>backward 30</"
"userinput> in between are executed. The comments before the "
"<userinput>print</userinput> commands explain what they are doing. The "
"command <userinput>backward 30</userinput> is there to make sure every "
"output is on a new line. As you see variables can be used just as if their "
"where what they contain, you can use them with any kind of <link linkend="
"\"operators\">operators</link> or give them as input when invoking <link "
"linkend=\"commands\">commands</link>."
msgstr ""
"Molimo razmotrite sljedeći dio &turtlescript;: <screen>\n"
"$a = 2004\n"
"$b = 25\n"
"\n"
"# naredna komanda štampa \"2029\"\n"
"štampaj $a + $b\n"
"nazad 30\n"
"# naredna komanda štampa \"2004 plus 25 equals 2029\"\n"
"štampaj $a + \" plus \" + $b + \" equals \" + ($a + $b)\n"
"</screen> U prva dva reda promjenljive <userinput>$a</userinput> i "
"<userinput>$b</userinput> su namještene na 2004 i 25. Onda u dva "
"<userinput>štampaj</userinput> komande sa <userinput>nazad 30</userinput> "
"između su izvršene. Komentari prije <userinput>štampaj</userinput> komandi "
"objašnjavaju šta rade. Komanda <userinput>nazad 30</userinput> je tu da "
"osigura da je svaki izlaz u novom redu. Kao št vidite promjenljive se mogu "
"koristiti samo kao da su to što sadrže,  možete ih koristiti sa sa blo kojom "
"vrstom <link linkend=\"operators\">operatora</link> ili ih dati kao ulaz pri "
"pozivu <link linkend=\"commands\">komande</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One more example: <screen>\n"
"$name = ask \"What is your name?\"\n"
"print \"Hi \" + $name + \"! Good luck while learning the art of "
"programming...\"\n"
"</screen> Pretty straight forward. Again you can see that the variable "
"<userinput>$name</userinput>, treated just like a string."
msgstr ""
"Još jedan primjer: <screen>\n"
"$name = traži \"What is your name?\"\n"
"štampaj \"Hi \" + $name + \"! Good luck while learning the art of "
"programming...\"\n"
"</screen> Prilično pravo naprijed. Ponovo možete vidjeti da je promjenljiva "
"<userinput>$ime</userinput>, tretirana samo kao string."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When using variables the <link linkend=\"the-inspector\">inspector</link> is "
"very helpful. It shows you the contents of all variables that are currently "
"in use."
msgstr ""
"Kada koristite promjenljive <link linkend=\"the-inspector\">inspektor</link> "
"je od pomoći. On vam pokazuje sadržaje svih promjenljivih koje su trenutno u "
"upotrebi."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling execution"
msgstr "Kontrolisanje izvršenja"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The execution controllers enable you &mdash; as their name implies &mdash; "
"to control execution."
msgstr ""
"Upravljači izvršenja vam omogućuju &mdash; kao što im i ime implicira "
"&mdash; da upravljate izvršenjem."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Execution controlling commands are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with "
"dark green in a bold font type. The brackets are mostly used together with "
"execution controllers and they are <glossterm>highlighted</glossterm> with "
"black."
msgstr ""
"Komande za upravljanje izvršenjem  su <glossterm>označene</glossterm> tamno "
"zelenom u podebljanom tipu fonta. Zagrade se uglavnom koriste zajedno sa "
"upravljačima izvršenja i oni su <glossterm>označeni</glossterm> crnim."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid "Have the turtle wait"
msgstr "Natjerajte kornjaču da čeka"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have done some programming in &kturtle; you have might noticed that "
"the turtle can be very quick at drawing. This command makes the turtle wait "
"for a given amount of time."
msgstr ""
"Ukoliko ste radili neko programiranje u &kturtle; možda ste primijetili da "
"kornjače na crtežu mogu biti vrlo brze. Ova komanda čini da kornjača čeka "
"zadani iznos vremena."

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>wait</term>"
msgstr "<term>sačekaj</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>wait</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>sačekaj</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid "wait X"
msgstr "sačekaj X"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>wait</userinput> makes the turtle wait for X seconds. <screen>\n"
"repeat 36 {\n"
"  forward 5\n"
"  turnright 10\n"
"  wait 0.5\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> This code draws a circle, but the turtle will wait half a second "
"after each step. This gives the impression of a slow-moving turtle."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sačekaj</userinput> čini da kornjača čeka X sekundi. <screen>\n"
"ponovi 36 {\n"
"  naprijed 5\n"
"  desno 10\n"
" sačekaj 0.5\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Ovaj kod crta krug, ali kornjača će čekati pola sekunde nakon "
"svakog koraka. Ovo daje utisak sporo-kretajuće kornjače."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "Execute \"if\""
msgstr "Izvrši \"if\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>if</term>"
msgstr "<term>ako</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>if</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>ako</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid "if <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean</link> { ... }"
msgstr "ako <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulovo</link> { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The code that is placed between the brackets will only be executed "
"<userinput>if</userinput> the <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean value</"
"link> evaluates <quote>true</quote>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 6\n"
"if $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  print \"$x is greater than five!\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> On the first line <userinput>$x</userinput> is set to 6. On the "
"second line a <link linkend=\"comparing-operators\">comparing operator</"
"link> is used to evaluate <userinput>$x &gt; 5</userinput>. Since this "
"evaluates <quote>true</quote>, 6 is larger than 5, the execution controller "
"<userinput>if</userinput> will allow the code between the brackets to be "
"executed."
msgstr ""
"Kod koji je smješten između zagrada bit će izvršen samo <userinput>ako je</"
"userinput> <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulova vrijednost</"
"link>evaluirana kao <quote>tačno</quote>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 6\n"
"ako $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  štampaj \"$x is greater than five!\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Na prvoj liniji <userinput>$x</userinput> je namješten na 6. Na "
"drugoj liniji <link linkend=\"comparing-operators\">operator poređenja</"
"link> se koristi da se evaluira <userinput>$x &gt; 5</userinput>. Pošto se "
"evaluira kao <quote>tačno</quote>, 6 je veće od 5, kontrolor izvršenja "
"<userinput>ako</userinput> će dozvoliti da se izvrši kod između zagrada."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid "If not, in other words: \"else\""
msgstr "Ako ne, drugim riječima: \"else\""

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>else</term>"
msgstr "<term>inače</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>else</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>inače</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid "if <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean</link> { ... } else { ... }"
msgstr ""
"ako <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulovo</link> { ... } inače { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>else</userinput> can be used in addition to the execution "
"controller <link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>if</userinput></link>. The code "
"between the brackets after <userinput>else</userinput> is only executed if "
"the <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean</link> evaluates <quote>false</"
"quote>. <screen>\n"
"reset\n"
"$x = 4\n"
"if $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  print \"$x is greater than five!\"\n"
"} else {\n"
"  print \"$x is smaller than six!\"\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> The <link linkend=\"comparing-operators\">comparing operator</"
"link> evaluates the expression <userinput>$x &gt; 5</userinput>. Since 4 is "
"not greater than 5 the expression evaluates <quote>false</quote>. This means "
"the code between the brackets after <userinput>else</userinput> gets "
"executed."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>inače</userinput> se može koristiti kao dodatak upravljačima "
"izvršenja <link linkend=\"if\"><userinput>ako</userinput></link>. Kod između "
"zagrada nakon <userinput>inače</userinput> se izvršava samo ako je <link "
"linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulova</link> evaluirana kao<quote>pogrešno</"
"quote>. <screen>\n"
"resetuj\n"
"$x = 4\n"
"ako $x &gt; 5 {\n"
"  štampaj \"$x is greater than five!\"\n"
"} inače {\n"
"  štampaj \"$x is smaller than six!\". }\n"
"</screen> The <link linkend=\"comparing-operators\">operator poređenja</"
"link>  računa izraz <userinput>$x &gt; 5</userinput>. Pošto 4 nije veće od 5 "
"izraz ima vrijednost <quote>netačni</quote>. To znači da se kod između "
"zagrada nakon <userinput>inače</userinput> izvršava."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"while\" loop"
msgstr "\"while\" petlja"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>while</term>"
msgstr "<term>dok</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>while</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>dok</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid "while <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean</link> { ... }"
msgstr "dok <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulova</link> { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The execution controller <userinput>while</userinput> is a lot like <link "
"linkend=\"if\"><userinput>if</userinput></link>. The difference is that "
"<userinput>while</userinput> keeps repeating (looping) the code between the "
"brackets until the <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean</link> evaluates "
"<quote>false</quote>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 1\n"
"while $x &lt; 5 {\n"
"  forward 10\n"
"  wait 1\n"
"  $x = $x + 1\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> On the first line <userinput>$x</userinput> is set to 1. On the "
"second line <userinput>$x &lt; 5</userinput> is evaluated. Since the answer "
"to this question is <quote>true</quote> the execution controller "
"<userinput>while</userinput> starts executing the code between the brackets "
"until the <userinput>$x &lt; 5</userinput> evaluates <quote>false</quote>. "
"In this case the code between the brackets will be executed 4 times, because "
"every time the fifth line is executed <userinput>$x</userinput> increases by "
"1."
msgstr ""
"Upravljač izvršenjem <userinput>dok</userinput> je dosta sličan <link "
"linkend=\"if\"><userinput>ako</userinput></link>. Razlika je da "
"<userinput>dok</userinput> stalno ponavlja kod između zagrada (pravi petlju) "
"dok se<link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulova</link> evaluira kao "
"<quote>pogrešno</quote>. <screen>\n"
"$x = 1\n"
"dok $x &lt; 5 {\n"
"  naprijed 10\n"
"  sačekaj 1\n"
"  $x = $x + 1\n"
"}. </screen>Na prvoj liniji <userinput>$x</userinput> je postavljen na 1. Na "
"drugoj liniji <userinput>$x &lt; 5</userinput> se računa. Pošto je odgovor "
"na ovo pitanje <quote>tačno</quote> izvršni kontroler <userinput>dok</"
"userinput> počinje izvršenje koda u zagradama sve dok <userinput>$x &lt; 5</"
"userinput> ne postane <quote>netačno</quote>. U tom slučaju, kod između "
"zagrada će se izvršiti 4 puta,jer svaki put kada se peta linija izvrši "
"<userinput>$x</userinput> se uveća za  1."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"repeat\" loop"
msgstr "\"repeat\" petlja"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>repeat</term>"
msgstr "<term>ponovi</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>repeat</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>ponovi</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid "repeat <link linkend=\"number\">number</link> { ... }"
msgstr "ponovi <link linkend=\"number\">broj</link> { ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The execution controller <userinput>repeat</userinput> is a lot like <link "
"linkend=\"while\"><userinput>while</userinput></link>. The difference is "
"that <userinput>repeat</userinput> keeps repeating (looping) the code "
"between the brackets for as many times as the given number."
msgstr ""
"Upravljač izvršenjem <userinput>ponovi</userinput> je dosta sličan <link "
"linkend=\"while\"><userinput>dok</userinput></link>. Razlika je da "
"<userinput>ponovi</userinput> stalno ponavlja kod između zagrada (pravi "
"petlju) onoliko puta koliki je zadani broj."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"for\" loop, a counting loop"
msgstr "\"for\" petlja, brojeća petlja"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>for</term>"
msgstr "<term>za</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>for</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>za</primary>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid "step"
msgstr "korak"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"for <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">variable</link> = <link "
"linkend=\"number\">number</link> to <link linkend=\"number\">number</link> "
"{ ... }"
msgstr ""
"za <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">promjenjivu</link> = <link "
"linkend=\"number\">broj</link> do <link linkend=\"number\">broj</link> "
"{ ... }"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>for</userinput> loop is a <quote>counting loop</quote>, &ie; "
"it keeps count for you. The first number sets the variable to the value in "
"the first loop. Every loop the number is increased until the second number "
"is reached. <screen>\n"
"for $x = 1 to 10 {\n"
"  print $x * 7\n"
"  forward 15\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Every time the code between the brackets is executed the "
"<userinput>$x</userinput> is increased by 1, until <userinput>$x</userinput> "
"reaches the value of 10. The code between the brackets prints the <userinput>"
"$x</userinput> multiplied by 7. After this program finishes its execution "
"you will see the times table of 7 on the canvas."
msgstr ""
"<userinput>za</userinput>petlja je <quote>brojeća petlja</quote>, &ie; ona "
"broji za vas. Prvi broj namješta promjenljivu na vrijednost u prvoj petlji. "
"Svakom petljom broj se povećava dok se ne dostigne drugi broj. <screen>\n"
"zar $x = 1 do 10 {\n"
"  štampaj $x * 7\n"
"  naprijed 15\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Svaki put kad se izvrši kod između zagrada <userinput>$x</"
"userinput> se poveća za 1, dok <userinput>$x</userinput> ne dostigne "
"vrijednost 10. Kod između zagrada štampa  <userinput>$x</userinput> "
"pomnoženo sa 7. Nakon što ovaj program završi svoje izvršenje vidjet ćete po "
"7 tabela za svaku vrijednost na platnu."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid "The default step size of a loop is 1, you can use an other value with"
msgstr ""
"Osnovna veličina koraka petlje je 1, vi možete koristiti neku drugu "
"vrijednost."

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"for <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">variable</link> = <link "
"linkend=\"number\">number</link> to <link linkend=\"number\">number</link> "
"step <link linkend=\"number\">number</link> { ... }"
msgstr ""
"za <link linkend=\"assignment-of-variables\">promjenljivu</link> = <link "
"linkend=\"number\">broj</link>do <link linkend=\"number\">broj</link> korak "
"<link linkend=\"number\">broj</link> { ... }"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid "Leave a loop"
msgstr "Napusti petlju"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>break</term>"
msgstr "<term>prekini</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>break</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>prekini</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>break</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>prekini</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Terminates the current loop immediately and transfers control to the "
"statement immediately following that loop."
msgstr ""
"Odmah prekida trenutnu petlju i prebacuje upravljanje na izjavu koja slijedi "
"neposredno iza te petlje."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stop executing your program"
msgstr "Zaustavite izvršenje vašeg programa"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>exit</term>"
msgstr "<term>izlaz</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>exit</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>izlaz</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screen>exit</screen>"
msgstr "<screen>izlaz</screen>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finishes the execution of your program."
msgstr "Završava izvršenje vašeg programa."

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:653
#, no-c-format
msgid "Checking assertions at runtime"
msgstr "Provjeravanje tvrdnji u dužini  trajanja"

#. Tag: term
#: programming-reference.docbook:656
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>assert</term>"
msgstr "<term>tvrditi</term>"

#. Tag: primary
#: programming-reference.docbook:656
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>assert</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>tvrditi</primary>"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "assert <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">boolean</link>"
msgstr "tvrdi <link linkend=\"boolean-value\">bulova</link>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can be used to reason about program or input correctness."
msgstr "Može se koristiti za prosuđivanje o programu ili tačnosti ulaza."

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:659
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$in = ask \"What is your year of birth?\"\n"
"# the year must be positive\n"
"assert $in > 0"
msgstr ""
"$in = traži \"What is your year of birth?\"\n"
"# godina mora biti pozitivna\n"
"tvrdi $in > 0"

#. Tag: title
#: programming-reference.docbook:687
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create your own commands with <quote>learn</quote>"
msgstr "Napravite svoju vlastitu komandu sa <quote>uči</quote>"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>learn</userinput> is special as it is used to create your own "
"commands. The commands you create can take <glossterm linkend=\"input-output"
"\">input</glossterm> and return <glossterm linkend=\"input-output\">output</"
"glossterm>. Let us take a look at how a new command is created: <screen>\n"
"learn circle $x {\n"
"  repeat 36 {\n"
"    forward $x\n"
"    turnleft 10\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> The new command is called <userinput>circle</userinput>. "
"<userinput>circle</userinput> takes one <glossterm linkend=\"input-output"
"\">input</glossterm> argument, to set the size of the circle. "
"<userinput>circle</userinput> returns no <glossterm linkend=\"input-output"
"\">output</glossterm>. The <userinput>circle</userinput> command can now be "
"used like a normal command in the rest of the code. See this example:"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>uči</userinput> je posebno pošto se koristi za pravljenje vaših "
"vlastitih komandi. Komande koje napravite mogu uzeti <glossterm linkend="
"\"input-output\">ulaz</glossterm> i vrati se <glossterm linkend=\"input-"
"output\">izlaz</glossterm>. Hajdemo sad pogledati kako se pravi nova "
"komanda: <screen>\n"
"uči krug $x {\n"
"  ponovi 36 {\n"
"    naprijed $x\n"
"    lijevo 10\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Nova komanda se zove <userinput>krug</userinput>. <userinput>krug</"
"userinput> uzima jedan <glossterm linkend=\"input-output\">ulazni </"
"glossterm> argument, da namjesti veličinu kruga. <userinput>krug</userinput> "
"ne vraća <glossterm linkend=\"input-output\">izlaz</glossterm>. "
"<userinput>krug</userinput> komanda se sad može koristiti kao  normalna "
"komanda u ostatku koda. Pogledajte ovaj primjer:"

#. Tag: screen
#: programming-reference.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"learn circle $X {\n"
"  repeat 36 {\n"
"    forward $X \n"
"    turnleft 10 \n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"go 200,200 \n"
"circle 20\n"
"\n"
"go 300,200 \n"
"circle 40"
msgstr ""
"uči krug $X {\n"
"  ponovi 36 {\n"
"    naprijed $X \n"
"    lijevo 10 \n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"idi 200,200"

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the next example, a command with a return value is created. <screen>\n"
"learn faculty $x {\n"
"  $r = 1\n"
"  for $i = 1 to $x {\n"
"    $r = $r * $i\n"
"  }\n"
"  return $r\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"print faculty 5\n"
"</screen> In this example a new command called <userinput>faculty</"
"userinput> is created. If the input of this command is <userinput>5</"
"userinput> then the output is <userinput>5*4*3*2*1</userinput>. By using "
"<userinput>return</userinput> the <glossterm linkend=\"input-output"
"\">output</glossterm> value is specified and the execution is returned."
msgstr ""
"U sljedećem primjeru pravi se komanda sa povratnom vrijednosti. <screen>\n"
"učite fakultet $x {\n"
"  $r = 1\n"
"  za $i = 1 to $x {\n"
"    $r = $r * $i\n"
"  }\n"
"  vrati se $r\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"štampaj fakultet 5\n"
"</screen> U ovom primjeru nova komanda koja se zove <userinput>fakultet</"
"userinput> je stvorena. Ako je ulaz ove komande <userinput>5</userinput> "
"onda je izlaz <userinput>5*4*3*2*1</userinput>. Koristeći <userinput>vrati "
"se</userinput> <glossterm linkend=\"input-output\">izlaz</glossterm> "
"vrijednost je specifiirana i vraćeno je izvršenje."

#. Tag: para
#: programming-reference.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Commands can have more than one <glossterm linkend=\"input-output\">input</"
"glossterm>. In the next example, a command that draws a rectangle is "
"created: <screen>\n"
"learn box $x, $y {\n"
"  forward $y\n"
"  turnright 90\n"
"  forward $x\n"
"  turnright 90\n"
"  forward $y\n"
"  turnright 90\n"
"  forward $x\n"
"  turnright 90\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Now you can run <userinput>box 50, 100</userinput> and the turtle "
"will draw a rectangle on the canvas."
msgstr ""
"Komande mogu imati više od jednog <glossterm linkend=\"input-output\">ulaza</"
"glossterm>. U sljedećem primjeru, napravljena je komanda koja crta pravi "
"ugao: <screen>\n"
"luči kutija $x, $y {\n"
"  naprijed $y\n"
"  desno 90\n"
"  naprijed $x\n"
" desno 90\n"
"  naprijed $y\n"
"  desno 90\n"
"  narijed $x\n"
"  desno 90\n"
"}\n"
"</screen> Sad možete okrenuti <userinput>kutija 50, 100</userinput> i "
"kornjača će crtati pravi ugao na platnu."
